IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P8-gate`

-- P8-art78: Article 78, confidentiality. LAYER 1.
-- Article 78 is in the group `Notified bodies, GPAI, governance, penalties and Art 78`, which applies from 2 August 2025 (Art 113), earlier than the group General of the other Articles of this part.
-- Article 78 has no `▼M1` passage in this part's range except that the footnote of paragraph 1(a) is residue of the text (lines 1285 to 1287).
-- Where a rule can bind any of several parties (the Commission, a market surveillance authority, a notified body, any other person), the party is an input of the rule.
-- The consolidated text is a rendering with no legal effect.

DECLARE `Art 78 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 78(1) respect the confidentiality of the information and data obtained in carrying out their tasks and activities`
    `Art 78(2) request data that is not strictly necessary for the assessment of the risk posed by AI systems and for the exercise of their powers`
    `Art 78(2) put in place adequate and effective cybersecurity measures to protect the security and confidentiality of the information and data obtained`
    `Art 78(2) delete the data collected as soon as it is no longer needed for the purpose for which it was obtained`
    `Art 78(3) disclose the information exchanged on a confidential basis without prior consultation of the originating national competent authority and the deployer`
    `Art 78(3) include sensitive operational data in the exchange of information`
    `Art 78(3) keep the technical documentation within the premises of the authority`
    `Art 78(3) ensure that the market surveillance authority can, upon request, immediately access the documentation or obtain a copy thereof`
    `Art 78(3) allow access to the documentation or any copy thereof to staff of the market surveillance authority who do not hold the appropriate level of security clearance`
    `Art 78(5) exchange confidential information with regulatory authorities of third countries`

DECLARE `Art 78(1) interest that the confidentiality protects` IS ONE OF
    `Art 78(1)(a) the intellectual property rights and confidential business information or trade secrets of a natural or legal person, including source code`
    `Art 78(1)(b) the effective implementation of this Regulation, in particular for the purposes of inspections, investigations or audits`
    `Art 78(1)(c) public and national security interests`
    `Art 78(1)(d) the conduct of criminal or administrative proceedings`
    `Art 78(1)(e) information classified pursuant to Union or national law`
    `Art 78(1) any other interest that the list does not name`

§ `Article 78(1): the duty of confidentiality and the interests it protects`

-- src:1284 | 1. The Commission, market surveillance authorities and notified bodies and any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation shall, in accordance with Union or national law, respect the confidentiality of information and data obtained in carrying out their tasks and activities in such a manner as to protect, in particular:
@ref Art 78(1) introductory words (src:1284)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party is the Commission, a market surveillance authority, a notified body or any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has obtained information and data in carrying out its tasks and activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(1) the party must respect the confidentiality of the information and data obtained in carrying out its tasks and activities` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group of Article 78 applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the party is the Commission, a market surveillance authority, a notified body or any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation` AND `the party has obtained information and data in carrying out its tasks and activities`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "The Commission, market surveillance authorities and notified bodies and any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation" and about "information and data obtained in carrying out their tasks and activities", with no "only"

-- src:1284 | 1. The Commission, market surveillance authorities and notified bodies and any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation shall, in accordance with Union or national law, respect the confidentiality of information and data obtained in carrying out their tasks and activities in such a manner as to protect, in particular:
@ref Art 78(1) introductory words (src:1284)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party` IS A `Arts 72 to 79 party`
      `the party is the Commission, a market surveillance authority, a notified body or any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has obtained information and data in carrying out its tasks and activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 78 act`
`Art 78(1) the party's duty to respect the confidentiality of the information and data obtained` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the party is the Commission, a market surveillance authority, a notified body or any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation`) OR (NOT `the party has obtained information and data in carrying out its tasks and activities`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed or barred: the group of Article 78 does not apply on the date asked, or the facts the rule is about do not all hold
    ELSE
        PARTY `the party`
        MUST `Art 78(1) respect the confidentiality of the information and data obtained in carrying out their tasks and activities`
        HENCE FULFILLED

-- line 1287 is `);`, the end of the footnote reference in point (a), and has no text of its own to quote
-- src:1284 | 1. The Commission, market surveillance authorities and notified bodies and any other natural or legal person involved in the application of this Regulation shall, in accordance with Union or national law, respect the confidentiality of information and data obtained in carrying out their tasks and activities in such a manner as to protect, in particular:
-- src:1285 | (a) the intellectual property rights and confidential business information or trade secrets of a natural or legal person, including source code, except in the cases referred to in Article 5 of Directive (EU) 2016/943 of the European Parliament and of the Council (
-- src:1286 | [^2]
-- src:1288 | (b) the effective implementation of this Regulation, in particular for the purposes of inspections, investigations or audits;
-- src:1289 | (c) public and national security interests;
-- src:1290 | (d) the conduct of criminal or administrative proceedings;
-- src:1291 | (e) information classified pursuant to Union or national law.
@ref Art 78(1) points (a) to (e) (src:1284-1286, src:1288-1291)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the interest` IS A `Art 78(1) interest that the confidentiality protects`
      `the case is one referred to in Article 5 of Directive (EU) 2016/943` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(1) the confidentiality that the party respects is to protect the interest` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group of Article 78 applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE CONSIDER `the interest`
         WHEN `Art 78(1) any other interest that the list does not name` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "in such a manner as to protect, in particular:" is followed by a list that no "only" closes
         WHEN `Art 78(1)(a) the intellectual property rights and confidential business information or trade secrets of a natural or legal person, including source code` THEN
             IF `the case is one referred to in Article 5 of Directive (EU) 2016/943`
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in the cases referred to in Article 5 of Directive (EU) 2016/943"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Article 78(2): what the authorities may request, protect and keep`

-- src:1292 | 2. The authorities involved in the application of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1 shall request only data that is strictly necessary for the assessment of the risk posed by AI systems and for the exercise of their powers in accordance with this Regulation and with Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. They shall put in place adequate and effective cybersecurity measures to protect the security and confidentiality of the information and data obtained, and shall delete the data collected as soon as it is no longer needed for the purpose for which it was obtained, in accordance with applicable Union or national law.
@ref Art 78(2) first sentence (src:1292)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the authority is involved in the application of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data is not strictly necessary for the assessment of the risk posed by AI systems and for the exercise of the authority's powers in accordance with this Regulation and with Regulation (EU) 2019/1020` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(2) first sentence the authority is barred from requesting data that is not strictly necessary for the assessment of the risk posed by AI systems and for the exercise of its powers` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group of Article 78 applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the authority is involved in the application of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1` AND `the data is not strictly necessary for the assessment of the risk posed by AI systems and for the exercise of the authority's powers in accordance with this Regulation and with Regulation (EU) 2019/1020`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall request only data that is strictly necessary for the assessment of the risk posed by AI systems and for the exercise of their powers" (a closed "only": a request for other data is barred)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is about authorities "involved in the application of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1" and about data that is not strictly necessary

-- src:1292 | 2. The authorities involved in the application of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1 shall request only data that is strictly necessary for the assessment of the risk posed by AI systems and for the exercise of their powers in accordance with this Regulation and with Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. They shall put in place adequate and effective cybersecurity measures to protect the security and confidentiality of the information and data obtained, and shall delete the data collected as soon as it is no longer needed for the purpose for which it was obtained, in accordance with applicable Union or national law.
@ref Art 78(2) first sentence (src:1292)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party` IS A `Arts 72 to 79 party`
      `the authority is involved in the application of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 78 act`
`Art 78(2) first sentence the authority's bar on requesting data that is not strictly necessary` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the authority is involved in the application of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed or barred: the group of Article 78 does not apply on the date asked, or the facts the rule is about do not all hold
    ELSE
        PARTY `the party`
        SHANT `Art 78(2) request data that is not strictly necessary for the assessment of the risk posed by AI systems and for the exercise of their powers`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the party` BECAUSE "the authority requested data that was not strictly necessary for the assessment of the risk posed by AI systems and for the exercise of its powers"

-- src:1292 | 2. The authorities involved in the application of this Regulation pursuant to paragraph 1 shall request only data that is strictly necessary for the assessment of the risk posed by AI systems and for the exercise of their powers in accordance with this Regulation and with Regulation (EU) 2019/1020. They shall put in place adequate and effective cybersecurity measures to protect the security and confidentiality of the information and data obtained, and shall delete the data collected as soon as it is no longer needed for the purpose for which it was obtained, in accordance with applicable Union or national law.
@ref Art 78(2) second sentence, cybersecurity (src:1292)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the authority has obtained information and data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(2) second sentence the authority must put in place adequate and effective cybersecurity measures to protect the security and confidentiality of the information and data obtained` MEANS
