§ `Article 78(3): information exchanged between national competent authorities and the Commission`

-- "shall not be disclosed without prior consultation of the originating national competent authority and the deployer when [high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities] and when [such disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests]".
-- src:1293 | 3. Without prejudice to paragraphs 1 and 2, information exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission shall not be disclosed without prior consultation of the originating national competent authority and the deployer when high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities and when such disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests. This exchange of information shall not cover sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities.
@ref Art 78(3) first subparagraph, first sentence (src:1293)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the information is exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the originating national competent authority and the deployer have been consulted before the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(3) first sentence the disclosure of the information without prior consultation is barred` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group of Article 78 applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF     `the information is exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission`
            AND `the high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities`
            AND `the disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests`
            AND (NOT `the originating national competent authority and the deployer have been consulted before the disclosure`)
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "information exchanged on a confidential basis ... shall not be disclosed without prior consultation of the originating national competent authority and the deployer when ... and when ..." (a flat negative: the bar holds)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is for information exchanged on a confidential basis, for the systems and authorities named, and where disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests; the text is silent otherwise

-- src:1293 | 3. Without prejudice to paragraphs 1 and 2, information exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission shall not be disclosed without prior consultation of the originating national competent authority and the deployer when high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities and when such disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests. This exchange of information shall not cover sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities.
@ref Art 78(3) first subparagraph, first sentence (src:1293)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the information is exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 78 act`
`Art 78(3) first sentence the national competent authority's bar on disclosing the information without prior consultation` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the information is exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission`) OR (NOT `the high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities`) OR (NOT `the disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is barred: the group of Article 78 does not apply on the date asked, or the facts the bar is about do not all hold
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party national competent authority`
        SHANT `Art 78(3) disclose the information exchanged on a confidential basis without prior consultation of the originating national competent authority and the deployer`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `Arts 72 to 79 party national competent authority` BECAUSE "the information was disclosed without prior consultation of the originating national competent authority and the deployer"

-- src:1293 | 3. Without prejudice to paragraphs 1 and 2, information exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission shall not be disclosed without prior consultation of the originating national competent authority and the deployer when high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities and when such disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests. This exchange of information shall not cover sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities.
@ref Art 78(3) first subparagraph, second sentence (src:1293)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the data is sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(3) second sentence the exchange of information is barred from covering the sensitive operational data` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group of Article 78 applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the data is sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This exchange of information shall not cover sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities" (a flat negative: the bar holds)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is about "sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities"

-- src:1293 | 3. Without prejudice to paragraphs 1 and 2, information exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission shall not be disclosed without prior consultation of the originating national competent authority and the deployer when high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III are used by law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities and when such disclosure would jeopardise public and national security interests. This exchange of information shall not cover sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities.
@ref Art 78(3) first subparagraph, second sentence (src:1293)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the information is exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 78 act`
`Art 78(3) second sentence the national competent authority's bar on including sensitive operational data` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)) OR (NOT `the information is exchanged on a confidential basis between the national competent authorities or between national competent authorities and the Commission`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is barred: the group of Article 78 does not apply on the date asked, or the facts the bar is about do not all hold
    ELSE
        PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party national competent authority`
        SHANT `Art 78(3) include sensitive operational data in the exchange of information`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `Arts 72 to 79 party national competent authority` BECAUSE "sensitive operational data in relation to the activities of law enforcement, border control, immigration or asylum authorities was included in the exchange of information"

-- The second subparagraph is about a high-risk AI system: its provider is a law enforcement, immigration or asylum authority. The gate is the group's, asked for the AI system.
-- src:1294 | When the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III, the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV shall remain within the premises of those authorities. Those authorities shall ensure that the market surveillance authorities referred to in Article 74(8) and (9), as applicable, can, upon request, immediately access the documentation or obtain a copy thereof. Only staff of the market surveillance authority holding the appropriate level of security clearance shall be allowed to access that documentation or any copy thereof.
@ref Art 78(3) second subparagraph, first sentence (src:1294)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(3) second subparagraph first sentence the technical documentation remains within the premises of the authorities` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 78 3
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group of Article 78 applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) can save a system placed earlier
         ELSE IF `the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III, the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV shall remain within the premises of those authorities" (an unmet "when" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (c))

-- src:1294 | When the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III, the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV shall remain within the premises of those authorities. Those authorities shall ensure that the market surveillance authorities referred to in Article 74(8) and (9), as applicable, can, upon request, immediately access the documentation or obtain a copy thereof. Only staff of the market surveillance authority holding the appropriate level of security clearance shall be allowed to access that documentation or any copy thereof.
@ref Art 78(3) second subparagraph, first sentence (src:1294)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 78 act`
`Art 78(3) second subparagraph first sentence the authority's duty to keep the technical documentation within its premises` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 78 3
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF (NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)) OR (NOT `the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III`)
         THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group of Article 78 does not apply to the AI system on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
         ELSE
             PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party provider`
             MUST `Art 78(3) keep the technical documentation within the premises of the authority`
             HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1294 | When the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III, the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV shall remain within the premises of those authorities. Those authorities shall ensure that the market surveillance authorities referred to in Article 74(8) and (9), as applicable, can, upon request, immediately access the documentation or obtain a copy thereof. Only staff of the market surveillance authority holding the appropriate level of security clearance shall be allowed to access that documentation or any copy thereof.
@ref Art 78(3) second subparagraph, second sentence (src:1294)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(3) second subparagraph second sentence the authorities must ensure that the market surveillance authorities can, upon request, immediately access the documentation or obtain a copy thereof` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 78 3
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group of Article 78 applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) can save a system placed earlier
         ELSE IF `the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers ..., Those authorities shall ensure that the market surveillance authorities ... can, upon request, immediately access the documentation" (an unmet "when" gate counts as the text's no: ruling (c)) (fork F-78-3-second-sub-second-duty)

-- src:1294 | When the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III, the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV shall remain within the premises of those authorities. Those authorities shall ensure that the market surveillance authorities referred to in Article 74(8) and (9), as applicable, can, upon request, immediately access the documentation or obtain a copy thereof. Only staff of the market surveillance authority holding the appropriate level of security clearance shall be allowed to access that documentation or any copy thereof.
@ref Art 78(3) second subparagraph, second sentence (src:1294)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 78 act`
`Art 78(3) second subparagraph second sentence the authority's duty to ensure that the market surveillance authority can access the documentation` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 78 3
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF (NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)) OR (NOT `the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III`)
         THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the group of Article 78 does not apply to the AI system on the date asked, or the conditions of the duty are not met
         ELSE
             PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party provider`
             MUST `Art 78(3) ensure that the market surveillance authority can, upon request, immediately access the documentation or obtain a copy thereof`
             HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:1294 | When the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III, the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV shall remain within the premises of those authorities. Those authorities shall ensure that the market surveillance authorities referred to in Article 74(8) and (9), as applicable, can, upon request, immediately access the documentation or obtain a copy thereof. Only staff of the market surveillance authority holding the appropriate level of security clearance shall be allowed to access that documentation or any copy thereof.
@ref Art 78(3) second subparagraph, third sentence (src:1294)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documentation is the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV of a high-risk AI system referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III whose provider is a law enforcement, immigration or asylum authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member of staff of the market surveillance authority holds the appropriate level of security clearance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(3) second subparagraph third sentence the member of staff is barred from accessing the documentation or any copy thereof` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 78 3
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group of Article 78 applies from the date Art 113 gives, and Art 111(2) can save a system placed earlier
         ELSE IF `the documentation is the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV of a high-risk AI system referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III whose provider is a law enforcement, immigration or asylum authority` AND (NOT `the member of staff of the market surveillance authority holds the appropriate level of security clearance`)
              THEN JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Only staff of the market surveillance authority holding the appropriate level of security clearance shall be allowed to access that documentation or any copy thereof" (a closed "only": others are barred)
              ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about that documentation, and a member of staff with the clearance is not said to be allowed by this sentence alone

-- src:1294 | When the law enforcement, immigration or asylum authorities are providers of high-risk AI systems referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III, the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV shall remain within the premises of those authorities. Those authorities shall ensure that the market surveillance authorities referred to in Article 74(8) and (9), as applicable, can, upon request, immediately access the documentation or obtain a copy thereof. Only staff of the market surveillance authority holding the appropriate level of security clearance shall be allowed to access that documentation or any copy thereof.
@ref Art 78(3) second subparagraph, third sentence (src:1294)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the route to high-risk` IS A `Route to high-risk`
      `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` IS A DATE
      `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documentation is the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV of a high-risk AI system referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III whose provider is a law enforcement, immigration or asylum authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 78 act`
`Art 78(3) second subparagraph third sentence the market surveillance authority's bar on allowing access to staff without the clearance` MEANS
    IF `Arts 72 to 79 Article 2(2) cuts off the provision` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the products are covered by Union harmonisation legislation listed in Section B of Annex I` `the requirements for high-risk AI systems under this Regulation have been integrated in that Union harmonisation legislation` 78 3
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: Article 2(2): "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) with Section B products (seam S14, fork F-S14-reach)
    ELSE IF (NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies to the AI system` `the date asked` `the route to high-risk` `the date the AI system was placed on the market or put into service` `the AI system has been significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III`)) OR (NOT `the documentation is the technical documentation referred to in Annex IV of a high-risk AI system referred to in point 1, 6 or 7 of Annex III whose provider is a law enforcement, immigration or asylum authority`)
         THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is barred: the group of Article 78 (for the AI system) does not apply on the date asked, or the facts the bar is about do not all hold
         ELSE
             PARTY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority`
             SHANT `Art 78(3) allow access to the documentation or any copy thereof to staff of the market surveillance authority who do not hold the appropriate level of security clearance`
             HENCE FULFILLED
             LEST BREACH BY `Arts 72 to 79 party market surveillance authority` BECAUSE "access was allowed to staff of the market surveillance authority who do not hold the appropriate level of security clearance"

§ `Article 78(4) and (5): savings, and exchange with third countries`

-- src:1295 | 4. Paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 shall not affect the rights or obligations of the Commission, Member States and their relevant authorities, as well as those of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings, including in the context of cross-border cooperation, nor shall they affect the obligations of the parties concerned to provide information under criminal law of the Member States.
@ref Art 78(4) first limb (src:1295)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the matter is a right or obligation of the Commission, Member States and their relevant authorities, or of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings, including in the context of cross-border cooperation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(4) paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 do not affect the rights or obligations of the Commission, the Member States and their relevant authorities, and of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group of Article 78 applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the matter is a right or obligation of the Commission, Member States and their relevant authorities, or of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings, including in the context of cross-border cooperation`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 shall not affect the rights or obligations of the Commission, Member States and their relevant authorities, as well as those of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings" (a flat negative: paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 do not affect them)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving is about the rights and obligations the sentence names

-- src:1295 | 4. Paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 shall not affect the rights or obligations of the Commission, Member States and their relevant authorities, as well as those of notified bodies, with regard to the exchange of information and the dissemination of warnings, including in the context of cross-border cooperation, nor shall they affect the obligations of the parties concerned to provide information under criminal law of the Member States.
@ref Art 78(4) second limb (src:1295)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the matter is an obligation of the parties concerned to provide information under criminal law of the Member States` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(4) paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 do not affect the obligations of the parties concerned to provide information under criminal law of the Member States` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group of Article 78 applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF `the matter is an obligation of the parties concerned to provide information under criminal law of the Member States`
         THEN JUST TRUE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nor shall they affect the obligations of the parties concerned to provide information under criminal law of the Member States" (a flat negative: paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 do not affect them)
         ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the saving is about the obligations the sentence names

-- src:1296 | 5. The Commission and Member States may exchange, where necessary and in accordance with relevant provisions of international and trade agreements, confidential information with regulatory authorities of third countries with which they have concluded bilateral or multilateral confidentiality arrangements guaranteeing an adequate level of confidentiality.
@ref Art 78(5) (src:1296)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the confidential information is exchanged with regulatory authorities of third countries with which the Commission or the Member State has concluded bilateral or multilateral confidentiality arrangements guaranteeing an adequate level of confidentiality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exchange is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exchange is in accordance with relevant provisions of international and trade agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 78(5) the Commission and the Member States may exchange confidential information with regulatory authorities of third countries` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`)
    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the group of Article 78 applies from the date Art 113 gives
    ELSE IF NOT `the confidential information is exchanged with regulatory authorities of third countries with which the Commission or the Member State has concluded bilateral or multilateral confidentiality arrangements guaranteeing an adequate level of confidentiality`
         THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is for exchange "with regulatory authorities of third countries with which they have concluded bilateral or multilateral confidentiality arrangements guaranteeing an adequate level of confidentiality", with no "only" (ruling (c))
         ELSE IF `the exchange is necessary` AND `the exchange is in accordance with relevant provisions of international and trade agreements`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may exchange, where necessary and in accordance with relevant provisions of international and trade agreements" (a "may" gated by "where": split site (ii), fork F-78-5-where)

-- src:1296 | 5. The Commission and Member States may exchange, where necessary and in accordance with relevant provisions of international and trade agreements, confidential information with regulatory authorities of third countries with which they have concluded bilateral or multilateral confidentiality arrangements guaranteeing an adequate level of confidentiality.
@ref Art 78(5) (src:1296)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the party` IS A `Arts 72 to 79 party`
      `the confidential information is exchanged with regulatory authorities of third countries with which the Commission or the Member State has concluded bilateral or multilateral confidentiality arrangements guaranteeing an adequate level of confidentiality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exchange is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exchange is in accordance with relevant provisions of international and trade agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Arts 72 to 79 party` `Art 78 act`
`Art 78(5) the party's choice to exchange confidential information with regulatory authorities of third countries` MEANS
    IF     (NOT (`Art 78 the group of Article 78 applies on the date asked` `the date asked`))
        OR (NOT `the confidential information is exchanged with regulatory authorities of third countries with which the Commission or the Member State has concluded bilateral or multilateral confidentiality arrangements guaranteeing an adequate level of confidentiality`)
        OR (NOT `the exchange is necessary`)
        OR (NOT `the exchange is in accordance with relevant provisions of international and trade agreements`)
    THEN FULFILLED  -- nothing is permitted: the group of Article 78 does not apply on the date asked, or a condition of the power is not met
    ELSE
        PARTY `the party`
        MAY `Art 78(5) exchange confidential information with regulatory authorities of third countries`
        HENCE FULFILLED
